Initialize the per-instance `selected` field before every admitted return.

When actions are disabled, return nonzero from the entry handler so this
invocation has no return callback. Otherwise, get kernel argument zero from the
outer register frame, treat it as the saved native syscall registers, and read
the userspace path from `di`. Let the supplied helper perform the bounded
no-fault copy and exact comparison.

The return handler reads the same instance data, obtains the result through
`regs_return_value()`, and marks exactly one monotonic flag for a selected call.

Publish the borrowed state before `register_kretprobe()`. On registration
failure, clear it. On shutdown, call `unregister_kretprobe()` before clearing it.
